# Review boundaries for the Founder Alpha.
#
# These paths decide whether the security controls are enforced at all, so a change to any of them
# must be reviewed by the founder — never by the agent that wrote it. This file is itself one of
# the paths it protects (see .github/CODEOWNERS below).
#
# Enforcement note, stated honestly: GitHub only applies CODEOWNERS when branch protection (or a
# ruleset) requires "Require a review from Code Owners". Both rulesets and branch protection need
# repository administration, so this file is prepared and correct but NOT yet enforced — see
# docs/SECURITY_CONTROLS.md for the exact one-time administrator action. Without that setting this
# is a request for review, not a control; the enforced part today is
# security/POLICY_LOCK.json + backend/scripts/security/verify_policy_lock.py, which fails the
# Security job whenever one of these files changes without a reviewed lock update.

